I took part in one of these together with Google and Amazon.

97
00:06:08.135 --> 00:06:12.975
It is still ongoing. So, you can see a couple of Varna-specific

98
00:06:12.975 --> 00:06:15.495
cases over here.

99
00:06:15.495 --> 00:06:19.335
Now, how the entire trust framework is going to look like, as I

100
00:06:19.335 --> 00:06:22.935
mentioned, earlier today the cabinet published a law.

101
00:06:22.935 --> 00:06:26.685
So, all of these that you see is going to be elaborated in Bulgarian

102
00:06:27.815 --> 00:06:31.575
and the security requirements are already elaborated by ENISA.

103
00:06:31.575 --> 00:06:34.335
So, you can also check the two publications that are shared on the

104
00:06:34.335 --> 00:06:38.095
slide. I'm not going to get into that much detail because I have 3

105
00:06:38.095 --> 00:06:42.375
minutes remaining. I just want to assure you that for more than a

106
00:06:42.375 --> 00:06:47.655
decade before the introduction of eIDAS, which is the European law

107
00:06:47.655 --> 00:06:49.205
regulating digital identity,

108
00:06:50.535 --> 00:06:53.615
there have been hundreds of experts working on the applicable

109
00:06:53.615 --> 00:06:55.325
standards providing security

110
00:06:56.415 --> 00:07:01.855
of this innovation. And for example, we have standards such as this

111
00:07:01.855 --> 00:07:05.965
one, which basically is about injection attack detection.

112
00:07:06.375 --> 00:07:10.055
We have standards from other series related to presentation attack

113
00:07:10.055 --> 00:07:14.175
detection. And all of these, including zero-knowledge

114
00:07:14.175 --> 00:07:20.495
proof implementations, are trying to enable citizens to protect their

115
00:07:20.495 --> 00:07:24.615
identity, to have a self-sovereign identity without disclosing too

116
00:07:24.615 --> 00:07:26.295
many facts, just statements.

117
00:07:26.295 --> 00:07:29.335
So, if I want to register in a casino, I'm not going to provide any

118
00:07:29.335 --> 00:07:33.335
data to the casino apart from a pure statement that, based on the

119
00:07:33.335 --> 00:07:36.495
data in the credentials in my wallet, I am above 18.

120
00:07:36.495 --> 00:07:40.095
Nothing else is needed for the casino owner to know and accept me

121
00:07:40.095 --> 00:07:42.685
into his platform or into his premises.

122
00:07:43.775 --> 00:07:48.285
Now, my conclusions about the risks, including in cybersecurity

123
00:07:48.815 --> 00:07:53.535
related areas. I'm also working in a special task force under the

124
00:07:53.535 --> 00:07:58.735
European Commission that is about to present the best practices in

125
00:07:58.735 --> 00:08:03.015
the field of DNS security for the obliged entities under NIS 2.

126
00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:06.095
So, I took two examples from this special task force.

127
00:08:06.095 --> 00:08:11.817
One example is the so-called DNS camel, which means that whenever on

128
00:08:11.817 --> 00:08:15.207
the red curve new requirements for security are presented,

129
00:08:15.697 --> 00:08:17.857
actually the level of security drops down.

130
00:08:17.857 --> 00:08:21.297
So, it becomes like a camel simply because we lose people.

131
00:08:21.297 --> 00:08:24.737
We lose people, competent people working for good companies

132
00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:29.857
who simply cannot provide the additional burden of ensuring and

133
00:08:29.857 --> 00:08:32.577
securing and double and triple checking.

134
00:08:32.577 --> 00:08:36.777
But then again, the curve goes up when the market,

135
00:08:36.777 --> 00:08:40.497
you know, finds its way towards the new requirement.

136
00:08:40.497 --> 00:08:43.657
And then again, a new requirement kicks in and then the curve goes

137
00:08:43.657 --> 00:08:48.377
back. So, the more measures you provide to secure a system does not

138
00:08:48.377 --> 00:08:51.137
mean that the system would be more secure.

139
00:08:51.137 --> 00:08:55.297
Many times the system actually gets less secure because fewer

140
00:08:55.297 --> 00:08:59.057
companies remain in the production, in the delivery pipeline.

141
00:08:59.057 --> 00:09:03.297
So, you have vendor lock-in, which is never too good,

142
00:09:03.297 --> 00:09:08.257
especially if we are evangelizing open innovation and free market

143
00:09:08.257 --> 00:09:12.577
principles. And the second concept with which I'm concluding

144
00:09:12.577 --> 00:09:16.417
is also related with my work in the DNS working group.

145
00:09:16.417 --> 00:09:20.417
So, we have good practices and standards in the field of DNS

146
00:09:20.417 --> 00:09:22.257
security. For those of you who are not aware,

147
00:09:22.257 --> 00:09:26.777
DNS is basically what brings the IP address to a human-readable

148
00:09:26.777 --> 00:09:30.297
format, our domain, so we know what is the digital identity of our

149
00:09:30.297 --> 00:09:35.297
websites. And DNS security, DNSSEC, is actually what authenticates

150
00:09:35.297 --> 00:09:38.017
this relation by signing the DNS records.

151
00:09:38.017 --> 00:09:40.567
Now, this exists from 2005.

152
00:09:41.537 --> 00:09:43.937
And the current uptake in the European Union,

153
00:09:43.937 --> 00:09:47.297
which is one of the greatest across the world,

154
00:09:47.297 --> 00:09:49.327
is actually less than 30%.

155
00:09:49.937 --> 00:09:55.657
So, less than 35% have a validation opportunity to check DNS

156
00:09:55.657 --> 00:10:00.977
records. And less than 10% in Bulgaria of websites have actually DNS

157
00:10:00.977 --> 00:10:03.777
security they can validate, but the validation shows there is no

158
00:10:03.777 --> 00:10:08.337
such record. What I'm trying to say here is that sometimes if these

159
00:10:08.337 --> 00:10:11.978
things are not enforced, they're just good practices and in the

160
00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:14.498
field of wallets, this is the greatest risk.

161
00:10:14.498 --> 00:10:18.538
So, there would be an option for you when coming to Varna to

162
00:10:18.538 --> 00:10:23.138
actually rent a boat, basically identify yourself towards the

163
00:10:23.138 --> 00:10:27.258
merchant, if you have a captain's license, to even present the

164
00:10:27.258 --> 00:10:30.658
captain's license together with authenticating the payment for

165
00:10:30.658 --> 00:10:35.378
renting the boat, and then with a simple biometric step to

166
00:10:35.378 --> 00:10:39.298
validate that you're the authenticated person who owns the

167
00:10:39.298 --> 00:10:42.378
wallet, who has the captain's license, who's doing the payment

168
00:10:42.378 --> 00:10:45.298
towards the bank, actually complete the process.

169
00:10:45.298 --> 00:10:48.658
Everything what I'm just showing you is going to be enabled by the

170
00:10:48.658 --> 00:10:54.338
wallets if actually this is enforced, because currently none of

171
00:10:54.338 --> 00:10:58.218
the existing documentation that I showed you on previous slides is

172
00:10:58.218 --> 00:11:01.458
enforcing the fact that the Bulgarian national digital identity

173
00:11:01.458 --> 00:11:05.538
wallet will need to be able to work with this type of strong

174
00:11:05.538 --> 00:11:08.618
customer authentication credentials coming from the banking, from the

175
00:11:08.618 --> 00:11:13.178
finance world. So, this would be a very nice presentation on paper

176
00:11:13.178 --> 00:11:16.298
and it can exist in France, in Germany, but in Bulgaria,

177
00:11:16.298 --> 00:11:20.938
it can be basically just a mirage simply because it's not enforced.

178
00:11:20.938 --> 00:11:24.498
So, too many security measures, over-security,

179
00:11:24.498 --> 00:11:27.378
overcomplicating things can be bad for business,

180
00:11:27.378 --> 00:11:31.818
but just producing opportunities, producing additional features

181
00:11:31.818 --> 00:11:34.818
which are not enforced can also be equally bad.

182
00:11:34.818 --> 00:11:38.578
With this, I'm leaving you with an open mind.

183
00:11:38.578 --> 00:11:41.808
Be aware that apart from the digital identity wallets for citizens,

184
00:11:42.218 --> 00:11:46.538
in 12 to 24 months, we'll also have the same wallets but for

185
00:11:46.538 --> 00:11:50.218
businesses, and start developing applications for your clients right

186
00:11:50.218 --> 00:11:52.138
now if you want to be among the first on the market.

187
00:11:52.138 --> 00:11:53.038
Thank you.
